WEBVTT

00:30.322 --> 00:33.951
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

00:44.044 --> 00:46.879
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION
SOME SCENES WERE GENERATED USING AI

00:46.880 --> 00:48.966
CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
WERE FILMED SAFELY

00:57.391 --> 00:58.934
You lying bastard!

01:04.106 --> 01:06.357
What are you gonna do
about my precious money?

01:06.358 --> 01:08.609
What are you gonna do about my 15 million?

01:08.610 --> 01:10.570
Oh, no. What do we do?

01:10.571 --> 01:12.197
Oh, no.

01:13.073 --> 01:14.448
Are you okay?

01:14.449 --> 01:16.909
Mr. Park! What are you doing?

01:16.910 --> 01:20.955
The insurance company told me
that I have angina,

01:20.956 --> 01:22.249
not myocardial infarction!

01:23.000 --> 01:25.126
And they won't cover angina.

01:25.127 --> 01:29.464
- You did this just because of that?
- "Just because of that"? Wow.

01:30.257 --> 01:31.925
So 15 million is a joke to you?

01:33.969 --> 01:37.305
When angina progresses,
it becomes a myocardial infarction.

01:37.306 --> 01:38.514
Exactly!

01:38.515 --> 01:40.475
So it wasn't a myocardial infarction!

01:41.226 --> 01:44.395
You should've just given me
antacids like I said,

01:44.396 --> 01:46.147
so I could've gone
to the hospital next morning!

01:46.148 --> 01:48.733
Why the hell did you cause
such a scene with the chopper?

01:48.734 --> 01:51.861
I'm out 15 million
and can't even get my insurance payout.

01:51.862 --> 01:55.240
If I had prescribed you antacids
and let you wait to go to the hospital,

01:56.450 --> 01:57.617
you would've gotten it.

02:00.370 --> 02:01.787
As a life insurance payout.

02:01.788 --> 02:03.831
- What are you saying?
- What?

02:03.832 --> 02:05.166
No…

02:05.167 --> 02:06.710
Life insurance?

02:08.170 --> 02:09.837
You goddamn quack!

02:09.838 --> 02:12.381
Mr. Park! Let's talk it out!

02:12.382 --> 02:14.343
- Let go!
- Let go of…

02:15.677 --> 02:17.053
- You…
-  Mr. Park.

02:17.054 --> 02:19.680
There seems to be a misunderstanding.

02:19.681 --> 02:21.807
We'll check on the situation first

02:21.808 --> 02:23.309
and…

02:23.310 --> 02:25.520
We're really sorry! Just a second!

02:26.897 --> 02:27.939
Hey!

02:28.440 --> 02:30.316
Where do you think you're going?

02:30.317 --> 02:32.360
You lying quack!

02:32.361 --> 02:34.570
Give me back my 15 million!

02:59.513 --> 03:02.973
EPISODE 3
GETTING THROUGH ANOTHER DAY

03:02.974 --> 03:06.060
Oh, my. This is bad.

03:06.061 --> 03:09.271
Mr. Park's normally such a gentleman,

03:09.272 --> 03:13.401
but once you get into a fight with him,
he never lets it go.

03:13.402 --> 03:16.153
He's like a bulldog gnawing on a bone.

03:20.242 --> 03:23.160
Anyway, you're really in for it, Dr. Do.

03:23.161 --> 03:24.620
CLIFFSIDE RAW FISH RESTAURANT

03:24.621 --> 03:25.704
- Auntie.
- We're here.

03:25.705 --> 03:27.039
Goodness.

03:27.040 --> 03:29.583
I'm sorry to tell you this…

03:29.584 --> 03:30.961
What is it?

03:31.670 --> 03:34.004
We're all out of ingredients.

03:34.005 --> 03:35.381
- You're…
- What?

03:35.382 --> 03:37.508
You're all out of ingredients?

03:37.509 --> 03:42.138
You told us to come over
for pork cutlets just 20 minutes ago.

03:42.139 --> 03:43.472
Exactly.

03:43.473 --> 03:47.310
I swear everything was fine
20 minutes ago, but…

03:50.230 --> 03:52.524
- Hello, Mr. Park.
- Hello.

03:54.443 --> 03:57.154
That's just how the world works.

03:57.654 --> 03:58.655
Isn't it?
:cue

04:03.160 --> 04:07.913
Just a week ago, I myself would have
never guessed that I'd be down 15 million.

04:07.914 --> 04:09.458
You know?

04:13.587 --> 04:16.088
I think it's because of me,
so I'll eat on my own.

04:16.089 --> 04:17.090
We're good now, right?

04:17.883 --> 04:19.968
- Enjoy your meals.
-  I'll go with him.

04:20.760 --> 04:22.470
I'll see you later.

04:22.471 --> 04:23.722
Oh, dear.

04:26.433 --> 04:29.060
GENERAL GOODS FOR SALE

04:31.146 --> 04:32.147
Gosh.

04:36.985 --> 04:39.111
Why did you come with me?

04:39.112 --> 04:41.114
What if Mr. Park starts gunning for you?

04:42.407 --> 04:44.242
Maybe I'll be the one gunning for him.

04:46.453 --> 04:47.871
Don't worry.

04:55.295 --> 04:56.379
Do you regret it?

04:58.173 --> 05:00.967
Do you wish you'd just
pretended not to notice and let him go?

05:03.553 --> 05:07.098
Whether I regret it or not is irrelevant.

05:08.016 --> 05:10.769
Because like him or not,
lacerations are lacerations?

05:13.939 --> 05:16.941
I'm sure Mr. Park
just lost his temper momentarily

05:16.942 --> 05:19.152
because of the sudden massive bill.

05:19.653 --> 05:21.570
I'm sure he'll let up soon.

05:21.571 --> 05:24.031
What more could he possibly do?

05:24.032 --> 05:25.158
Hmm?

05:34.668 --> 05:35.752
Turns out

05:36.670 --> 05:38.045
there was more he could do.

05:38.046 --> 05:39.380
Goodness me.

05:39.381 --> 05:42.633
Thank you all
for your hard work in the rain.

05:42.634 --> 05:43.717
You're here?

05:43.718 --> 05:45.302
Please don't mention it.

05:45.303 --> 05:49.890
This is the kind of work
we should be doing for our residents.

05:49.891 --> 05:51.893
Well, lookee here.

05:52.519 --> 05:54.103
Dr. Do Jiui.

05:54.104 --> 05:56.981
You're a proper garbage man.

05:56.982 --> 06:01.151
Sure would've been nice
if you had just done that from the start.

06:01.152 --> 06:02.945
That way I'd still have 15 million.

06:04.197 --> 06:05.739
Right.

06:07.993 --> 06:09.578
I can't take this anymore.

06:12.747 --> 06:13.873
Are you okay?

06:13.874 --> 06:15.332
What was that for?

06:15.333 --> 06:18.252
- I thought a fight was going to--
-  What?

06:18.253 --> 06:19.795
Do you have something to say?

06:19.796 --> 06:22.006
It's nothing. You take care now.

06:22.007 --> 06:23.549
Of course, he has nothing to say.

06:23.550 --> 06:25.135
Nothing to say, right?

06:26.803 --> 06:28.762
Just try to bear with it.

06:28.763 --> 06:30.723
I'm sure he's just frustrated.

06:30.724 --> 06:33.768
Why do you keep telling me
to bear with it?

06:34.519 --> 06:36.521
What did I do wrong just now?

06:37.230 --> 06:40.900
This is the least we could do for them.
They're the residents, after all.

06:40.901 --> 06:42.276
No.

06:42.277 --> 06:44.486
I won't stand for this anymore.

06:44.487 --> 06:45.864
I have no reason to!

06:55.624 --> 06:58.500
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

07:04.924 --> 07:08.636
Goodness. Look how inconvenient
things are for the both of us,

07:08.637 --> 07:11.889
because you'll only prescribe me
three days' worth of medicine.

07:11.890 --> 07:13.515
Your cough isn't getting better.

07:13.516 --> 07:15.977
Maybe because the doctor
is bad at his job.

07:17.896 --> 07:22.232
Do you take any other medication
or have you fallen ill before?

07:22.233 --> 07:23.484
Let's see…

07:23.485 --> 07:24.486
No.

07:27.447 --> 07:30.450
Let me take a look in your mouth.
Would you say "Ah" for me?

07:34.371 --> 07:36.081
I'll also take your temperature.

07:36.581 --> 07:38.332
For the love of…

07:38.333 --> 07:40.710
What's with all the prodding and poking?

07:41.544 --> 07:43.379
Chronic coughs are a bad sign.

07:43.380 --> 07:46.382
It might be good
to go to the mainland and get an X-ray--

07:46.383 --> 07:49.594
Why are you so eager
to send patients off to the mainland?

07:50.470 --> 07:52.429
I'm not a sucker like the chief!

07:52.430 --> 07:55.891
I couldn't afford that
in my wildest dreams,

07:55.892 --> 07:57.351
so just give me my meds now!

07:57.352 --> 08:00.480
I'm not a vending machine
that just dispenses your medicine!

08:01.314 --> 08:02.399
What?
:cue

08:03.358 --> 08:04.401
Go wait outside.

08:06.069 --> 08:07.070
Okay.

08:11.783 --> 08:12.867
Allow me to explain--

08:15.620 --> 08:19.415
Hello, ma'am. What brings you in today?

08:19.416 --> 08:22.627
It's the same problem as always. My knees.

08:23.128 --> 08:24.211
Your knees?

08:24.212 --> 08:27.090
That's why I've captured these
and brought them with me.

08:27.757 --> 08:30.843
I heard these are amazing
for aching knees.

08:30.844 --> 08:32.928
Oh, ma'am!

08:32.929 --> 08:35.055
What are…

08:35.056 --> 08:36.432
What are those?

08:36.433 --> 08:38.434
What do you think?

08:38.435 --> 08:42.146
I brought them for bee sting therapy.
You know how to administer it, right?

08:43.314 --> 08:44.523
Gosh, ma'am.

08:44.524 --> 08:48.402
You're not meant to administer
bee sting therapy using actual bees.

08:48.403 --> 08:51.572
You're supposed to refine the venom
extracted from a honeybee

08:51.573 --> 08:53.408
and inject it using a needle.

08:53.950 --> 08:55.659
So please put that away.

08:55.660 --> 08:58.912
Well, damn.
That was a total waste of time and effort.

09:01.416 --> 09:04.294
Ma'am, you'll have to take this with you.

09:05.003 --> 09:08.088
What use would I have for that?
It's not like I can eat it.

09:08.089 --> 09:10.175
But I can't eat it either…

09:11.926 --> 09:13.136
- Ms. Eom?
- Yes?

09:14.095 --> 09:15.847
Go take a seat and wait, please.

09:18.475 --> 09:19.476
What is it?

09:22.520 --> 09:24.480
Would you mind putting this away for me?

09:24.481 --> 09:26.565
You want me to put it away?

09:26.566 --> 09:27.775
Why's that?

09:27.776 --> 09:31.154
You think a country bumpkin like me
can handle bees with my bare hands?

09:32.197 --> 09:35.075
N-Not exactly.

09:38.620 --> 09:42.248
Fine. Your wish is my command,
your highness.

09:44.042 --> 09:45.250
Ooh…

09:45.251 --> 09:46.628
Cut it out.

09:48.671 --> 09:51.423
Seriously! I told you to cut it out!

09:51.424 --> 09:53.801
Just get out! What's wrong with you?

09:54.969 --> 09:57.514
Come on!

10:01.726 --> 10:03.770
It stings!

10:19.410 --> 10:20.662
It stings!

10:29.420 --> 10:31.131
I'm sorry, Ms. Eom.

10:34.884 --> 10:37.136
What's going on?

10:37.137 --> 10:39.139
-  Run!
-  Oh, you see…

10:39.889 --> 10:41.766
What is it?

10:47.438 --> 10:49.941
Run for your lives, everyone!

10:50.441 --> 10:53.278
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

10:57.699 --> 10:59.367
- That stings! Get out!
- The door!

11:00.618 --> 11:01.619
Run!

11:06.374 --> 11:08.125
- Stay away!
- Hurry!

11:08.126 --> 11:10.460
- Hurry!
- Stay still!

11:10.461 --> 11:11.462
- Here!
- Stay still!

11:12.380 --> 11:13.630
Stay still!

11:13.631 --> 11:15.132
That stings!

11:15.133 --> 11:17.259
Why are there bees in the center?

11:17.260 --> 11:19.470
- How on earth did this happen?
- Well…

11:22.098 --> 11:23.183
Hold on a minute.

11:23.808 --> 11:25.602
- What about Dr. Chiyeon?
- What?

11:26.394 --> 11:27.937
- Dr. Chiyeon.
- Huh?

11:28.479 --> 11:29.563
Huh?

11:34.235 --> 11:35.944
EXAM ROOM 2

11:56.466 --> 11:57.926
:cue

11:58.885 --> 12:00.594
That stings. Come on.

12:00.595 --> 12:02.012
Stay still.

12:02.013 --> 12:03.264
Seriously.

12:03.890 --> 12:07.018
Are you kidding me?
Look what they've done to my cute face.

12:07.727 --> 12:09.269
This is ridiculous.

12:09.270 --> 12:11.230
We got bees unleashed on us,

12:11.231 --> 12:14.233
but Ms. Sinhye's telling us
to just stay put.

12:14.234 --> 12:15.360
Of course, we should.

12:15.944 --> 12:17.569
We're civil servants.

12:17.570 --> 12:19.489
"Civil servants"?

12:20.198 --> 12:23.033
Well, if we're civil servants,

12:23.034 --> 12:25.495
they should at least
cover our expenses properly.

12:26.162 --> 12:29.206
I've been buying my needles
for the past few months.

12:29.207 --> 12:30.667
Self-funded needles!

12:31.501 --> 12:35.587
I know they don't cost that much,
but it really grinds my gears.

12:35.588 --> 12:37.882
- You shouldn't let that bother you.
- Why not?

12:38.466 --> 12:39.717
Because we're doctors.

12:40.802 --> 12:43.345
We shouldn't let money
get in the way of saving lives,

12:43.346 --> 12:44.429
as doctors.

12:44.430 --> 12:46.974
But still, this is a bit…

12:46.975 --> 12:48.101
It's unfair.

12:49.018 --> 12:50.770
But we're supposed to suck it up

12:51.813 --> 12:52.897
as soldiers.

12:53.523 --> 12:56.234
- You said we were civil servants.
- We are civil servants.

12:56.818 --> 12:58.236
We're also soldiers

12:59.487 --> 13:00.570
and doctors.

13:00.571 --> 13:01.905
Hmm…

13:01.906 --> 13:04.366
Sounds like a fancy way of saying
we're punching bags

13:04.367 --> 13:06.202
that the whole town can use.

13:09.455 --> 13:11.582
That's why you shouldn't try too hard.

13:13.543 --> 13:15.295
Nothing will come of it.

13:28.057 --> 13:32.687
Did something happen to him
before he came to Pyeondongdo?

13:33.271 --> 13:34.355
Uh…

13:35.398 --> 13:40.277
I heard he was sued by a resident
he treated before he came here.

13:41.571 --> 13:42.654
Someone sued him?

13:42.655 --> 13:45.575
Two patients with puffer fish poisoning
were brought in,

13:46.200 --> 13:51.039
but while he was treating one,
the other one apparently died of shock.

13:52.040 --> 13:56.376
And the family of the deceased
sued Dr. Hyeon.

13:56.377 --> 13:57.420
What? Are you…

13:58.463 --> 14:00.298
That's ridiculous.

14:01.007 --> 14:03.133
What's even more ridiculous

14:03.134 --> 14:06.596
is that the person who survived
also sued him.

14:07.180 --> 14:08.597
Why?

14:08.598 --> 14:10.807
I guess they chose
to side with their own people

14:10.808 --> 14:12.894
rather than the doctor
who saved their life.

14:15.229 --> 14:17.230
Even the person he trusted

14:17.231 --> 14:20.359
to be on his side
told Dr. Hyeon not to fight it.

14:26.282 --> 14:29.952
This is the least we could do for them.
They're the residents, after all.

14:30.953 --> 14:33.456
Is Ms. Hari also on the residents' side?

14:35.374 --> 14:37.126
EXAM ROOM

14:37.710 --> 14:39.544
Hello, sir. What brings you here--

14:39.545 --> 14:41.380
Prescribe this for me.

14:42.965 --> 14:44.800
- What?
- I don't have time.

14:44.801 --> 14:46.803
So just prescribe it for me now.

14:50.056 --> 14:51.599
GOPU SYRUP, PSEUDOPHEDINE…

14:55.311 --> 14:57.521
That's why you shouldn't try too hard.

14:57.522 --> 14:59.440
Nothing will come of it.

15:03.694 --> 15:05.028
I'll write you a script.

15:05.029 --> 15:07.155
GOPU SYRUP, PSEUDOPHEDINE

15:07.156 --> 15:10.075
Then, since you're
writing me a script anyway--

15:10.076 --> 15:12.661
I'll give you a lot.
Will 30 days' worth be enough?

15:12.662 --> 15:15.623
Hot damn. That sounds great.

15:16.249 --> 15:17.583
30-DAY PRESCRIPTION

15:18.709 --> 15:19.793
Please wait outside.

15:19.794 --> 15:20.878
Okay.

15:24.715 --> 15:25.883
Wasn't expecting that.

15:34.183 --> 15:36.561
True to the name, Pyeondongdo,

15:37.270 --> 15:40.397
where only one thing matters to them
and that is comfort,

15:40.398 --> 15:43.025
I decided to find comfort for myself.

15:43.609 --> 15:48.572
My insides are in a knot,
and I keep gagging.

15:48.573 --> 15:50.949
So I'm here to pick up
some digestive medicine.

15:50.950 --> 15:52.993
I'll write you your usual prescription.

15:52.994 --> 15:54.912
30-DAY PRESCRIPTION

15:57.999 --> 16:02.627
I need some pain relief patches
and some meds for my arthritis.
:cue

16:02.628 --> 16:04.714
Sure. Pick them up on your way out.

16:09.093 --> 16:12.929
I've got canker sores…

16:12.930 --> 16:14.932
I'll prescribe some Oremedy for you.

16:16.058 --> 16:19.311
Well, I don't care about the ointment.

16:19.312 --> 16:23.649
I was just wondering why I keep getting
so many canker sores…

16:24.317 --> 16:27.235
Think it's 'cause my immunity's shot?

16:27.236 --> 16:29.738
Do you think exercise
might make them heal?

16:29.739 --> 16:31.365
Exercise for immunity?

16:32.283 --> 16:33.533
Sure. It's great.

16:33.534 --> 16:34.743
You should exercise.

16:34.744 --> 16:37.412
I'm here to get some painkillers.

16:37.413 --> 16:40.041
Would you like Talenol or Iburonfen?

16:40.833 --> 16:42.877
Just give me whatever.

16:43.711 --> 16:44.837
I'll give you both.

16:45.880 --> 16:47.548
Oh… Okay.

16:58.935 --> 17:00.686
I'll prescribe you 30 days' worth.

17:01.479 --> 17:04.607
30

17:09.946 --> 17:11.571
You're right.

17:11.572 --> 17:13.031
They're both handsome.

17:13.032 --> 17:14.283
- Yes.
-  Yes.

17:18.704 --> 17:20.705
Here's thirty days' worth of medicine.

17:20.706 --> 17:23.541
Take them in the morning and evening,
30 minutes after a meal.

17:23.542 --> 17:27.630
Well, damn. That's more like it.

17:28.297 --> 17:31.800
So 3 times 1 is 3,
which makes it 11,000 won.

17:31.801 --> 17:34.135
-  Right.
-  Right.

17:34.136 --> 17:36.721
Only take them twice a day
in the morning and evening!

17:36.722 --> 17:38.265
-  Got it.
- Okay.

17:38.266 --> 17:40.601
- Take care!
- See you next time.

17:54.532 --> 17:56.157
Dr. Do.

17:56.158 --> 17:57.159
Yes?

17:57.827 --> 18:00.580
What's gotten into you recently?

18:02.498 --> 18:03.748
What do you mean?

18:03.749 --> 18:06.126
You prescribe whatever they ask for,

18:06.127 --> 18:08.378
and you send them away so quickly.

18:08.379 --> 18:11.590
And prescribing a month's worth
of cough medicine like that--

18:11.591 --> 18:14.051
You told me to let them have their way.

18:14.677 --> 18:17.179
- What?
- I was doing what you told me to do.

18:18.306 --> 18:22.518
I know now that getting into fights
will do me no good whatsoever.

18:23.728 --> 18:26.229
That's not what I--

18:26.230 --> 18:30.275
I just need to stick it out for a year,
then leave, safe and sound.

18:31.819 --> 18:35.364
Whatever happened to "Like them or not,
lacerations are lacerations?"

18:36.198 --> 18:38.075
I guess I adjusted to life here.

18:41.120 --> 18:42.121
I see.

18:42.705 --> 18:45.333
I get what kind of person you are now.

18:46.834 --> 18:47.917
What?

18:47.918 --> 18:50.963
I almost mistook you for a good doctor.

18:52.840 --> 18:54.175
I'm just a civil servant.

18:55.051 --> 18:57.969
Actually, I'm not even a civil servant.
What even am I?

18:57.970 --> 18:59.054
I'm nothing.

18:59.055 --> 19:01.056
That's why no one will protect me!

19:01.057 --> 19:03.100
I'm not done talking! Where are you going?

19:06.520 --> 19:07.521
Dr. Do.

19:08.314 --> 19:10.775
You'll have to make rounds
on Madeokdo tomorrow.

19:12.360 --> 19:14.569
- M-Madeokdo?
- Yes.

19:14.570 --> 19:17.364
Don't worry, though.
Ms. Yuk will be accompanying you.

19:17.365 --> 19:18.824
Ms. Hwang!

19:19.450 --> 19:22.745
Can I go to Madeokdo
with Dr. Hyeon instead?

19:24.705 --> 19:25.706
Me?

19:26.832 --> 19:29.250
Well, this would be
our first Madeokdo visit,

19:29.251 --> 19:31.461
so I figured it'd be awkward
for the patients

19:31.462 --> 19:33.713
if they're unacquainted
with both Dr. Do and me.

19:33.714 --> 19:36.174
Wouldn't Dr. Hyeon be better
since he's been there?

19:36.175 --> 19:37.759
Oh…

19:37.760 --> 19:39.928
But Dr. Hyeon said he doesn't want--

19:39.929 --> 19:41.097
I'll go.

19:42.139 --> 19:43.598
You're going to go on visits?

19:43.599 --> 19:45.058
Let's leave early tomorrow.

19:45.059 --> 19:46.519
Sure.

19:50.314 --> 19:51.774
I guess that settles that.

19:53.567 --> 19:55.527
You must be so happy, Dr. Do!

19:58.531 --> 20:01.200
What does she want from me?

20:04.161 --> 20:05.162
:cue

20:09.542 --> 20:11.419
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER
CLOSED

20:19.510 --> 20:20.593
START

20:20.594 --> 20:21.595
RECORD, STOP

21:12.438 --> 21:13.439
What the…

21:14.023 --> 21:17.609
It's not like I said anything wrong.
Why do I have to bear with everything?

21:23.991 --> 21:25.074
Hello?

21:25.075 --> 21:27.160
Dr. Jiui, where are you?

21:27.161 --> 21:29.746
The supplies we ordered are here.

21:29.747 --> 21:31.498
Could you pick them up for us?

21:31.499 --> 21:32.500
Thanks.

21:33.292 --> 21:34.752
Hey…

21:37.713 --> 21:39.131
I can't even…

21:39.840 --> 21:41.467
Only take what's yours!

21:42.134 --> 21:44.135
- Okay?
- Okay.

21:44.136 --> 21:46.347
You don't wanna take someone else's stuff.

21:46.889 --> 21:48.432
- This one's mine.
- Yeah.

21:53.103 --> 21:54.438
Looking for your delivery?

21:55.314 --> 21:56.315
Yes.

21:56.941 --> 21:58.400
Look hard.

21:59.193 --> 22:04.656
I've had hand tremors
ever since I lost 15 million.

22:04.657 --> 22:06.866
I might have dropped it somewhere.

22:06.867 --> 22:09.035
Those were supplies for the health center!

22:09.036 --> 22:11.079
That's none of my concern,

22:11.080 --> 22:13.666
just as my 15 million
was none of your concern.

22:18.337 --> 22:19.546
Oh!

22:19.547 --> 22:20.880
There it is.

22:20.881 --> 22:22.716
The delivery for the Public Health Center.

22:31.058 --> 22:35.896
On your way back,
drop off those remaining deliveries. Okay?

22:36.939 --> 22:38.064
What?

22:38.065 --> 22:39.984
They're all for old folks here.

22:40.734 --> 22:44.655
Isn't it a PH doc's duty to do everything
for the health of the residents?

22:46.782 --> 22:47.907
Isn't it?

22:47.908 --> 22:50.410
PYEONDONGDO VILLAGE HALL

22:50.411 --> 22:51.787
Use this if you want to.

22:55.833 --> 22:57.710
Are you sure that's yours?

23:07.469 --> 23:08.470
What are you doing?

23:09.054 --> 23:10.346
Ah…

23:10.347 --> 23:13.016
I'm putting on sunscreen.
I don't want to get burned.

23:13.017 --> 23:14.851
The sun's not even up yet though.

23:14.852 --> 23:17.187
Sunscreen's super important, you know.

23:18.063 --> 23:19.480
Oh…

23:19.481 --> 23:20.940
Do you want some?

23:25.446 --> 23:26.447
What is it?

23:27.781 --> 23:29.115
It's nothing.

23:29.116 --> 23:31.701
Come on. Put some on, okay?

23:31.702 --> 23:34.787
You're meant to apply it all the time.

23:34.788 --> 23:38.041
Early in the morning, late at night,
before bed and even during winter.

23:38.042 --> 23:39.667
No, really. I'm good.

23:39.668 --> 23:41.628
Don't play coy with me.

23:41.629 --> 23:43.671
Men wear it too nowadays.

23:43.672 --> 23:44.964
Give me your hand.

23:44.965 --> 23:46.050
Smear it all over.

23:47.384 --> 23:49.053
Don't miss any spots.

23:53.641 --> 23:56.226
No… Wait!

24:01.649 --> 24:03.067
Damn it.

24:09.114 --> 24:11.533
Seriously…

24:24.004 --> 24:25.880
HANDLE WITH CARE

24:25.881 --> 24:26.882
"Handle with care."

24:28.342 --> 24:29.802
"Handle with care."

24:33.889 --> 24:35.556
Yuk Ha…

24:35.557 --> 24:36.766
YUK HARI

24:36.767 --> 24:38.309
Ms. Yuk Hari.

24:38.310 --> 24:39.519
HANDLE WITH CARE
:cue

24:39.520 --> 24:40.729
"Handle with care"?

24:41.897 --> 24:46.484
In the spirit of handling it with care,
I should probably let her know.

24:46.485 --> 24:48.404
Yes, definitely.

24:49.279 --> 24:50.322
Let's see…

24:56.203 --> 24:59.873
Ms. Yuk, I came across your delivery
and it seemed important, so…

25:03.377 --> 25:05.713
What the…

25:06.547 --> 25:08.173
No!

25:09.216 --> 25:10.217
Delete.

25:10.968 --> 25:13.094
Come on. Delete.

25:13.095 --> 25:14.679
THIS MESSAGE HAS BEEN DELETED
FOR YOU ONLY

25:14.680 --> 25:16.098
No! Wait!

25:23.105 --> 25:25.357
What… What am I going to do?

25:26.191 --> 25:28.401
Come on!

25:28.402 --> 25:31.612
PYEONDONGDO, MADEOKDO, GAYEONGDO

25:34.283 --> 25:35.826
What the heck?

25:36.744 --> 25:38.287
- What is this?
- What's wrong?

25:39.163 --> 25:40.496
What?

25:40.497 --> 25:41.831
Uh…

25:41.832 --> 25:43.292
It's nothing.

25:47.755 --> 25:48.838
Oh, my.

25:48.839 --> 25:50.423
Thank you for coming.

25:50.424 --> 25:51.674
I'm the village chief.

25:53.677 --> 25:55.053
Goodness me.

25:55.054 --> 25:56.555
I guess you had a pretty rough trip.

25:57.139 --> 25:58.390
You're as pale as a ghost.

25:59.099 --> 26:01.852
- Excuse me?
- It's nothing. Come this way.

26:11.320 --> 26:13.321
You brought the packages?

26:13.322 --> 26:15.490
- Yes.
-  Well done.

26:15.491 --> 26:17.159
Now organize everything in there.

26:18.035 --> 26:19.620
Organize everything too?

26:28.003 --> 26:30.589
YUK HARI

26:37.096 --> 26:38.554
What brings you here today?

26:38.555 --> 26:43.935
Doctor, my boy, Juman,
normally eats like he's got a hollow leg,

26:43.936 --> 26:46.896
but today he hasn't touched
his food all day.

26:46.897 --> 26:48.857
Not even a drop of water.

26:50.025 --> 26:51.693
He has a hollow leg?

26:53.028 --> 26:56.948
He normally has a large appetite
but didn't even have a sip of water today.

26:56.949 --> 26:57.950
Ah…

26:58.575 --> 27:00.243
I'll need to examine the patient.

27:00.244 --> 27:02.829
Is he not able to come here?

27:02.830 --> 27:03.955
Oh, my.

27:03.956 --> 27:05.581
He's here with me.

27:05.582 --> 27:07.542
Goodness, Juman. Get out here.

27:07.543 --> 27:08.877
Goodness me.

27:10.129 --> 27:12.588
Please hurry and take a look at him.

27:12.589 --> 27:15.134
I'm worried my son might be sick!

27:20.639 --> 27:22.765
Goodness.

27:22.766 --> 27:24.267
You haven't treated him yet.

27:24.268 --> 27:26.352
Where are you going?

27:26.353 --> 27:31.357
MADEOKDO SENIOR CENTER

27:31.358 --> 27:33.860
That old woman, she's not exactly normal.

27:33.861 --> 27:36.362
She's not all there.

27:36.363 --> 27:39.449
She thinks that dog is her son
who died when he was little.

27:40.033 --> 27:42.077
Ah…

27:43.245 --> 27:44.246
Gosh.

27:46.665 --> 27:47.666
But…

27:49.334 --> 27:51.461
Oh, man.

28:00.095 --> 28:02.180
Bro, can you talk right now?

28:03.891 --> 28:06.851
Well, she's saying that her dog
won't eat or drink any water.

28:06.852 --> 28:08.395
What am I supposed to do?

28:10.606 --> 28:11.732
The weight?

28:12.774 --> 28:14.276
Around three kilos, I think?

28:16.403 --> 28:18.697
Okay, I'll get back to you later.

28:20.240 --> 28:21.658
Yeah.

28:22.409 --> 28:24.536
Juman…

28:31.668 --> 28:33.045
How's Juman doing?

28:34.755 --> 28:37.131
It's not serious, is it?

28:37.132 --> 28:40.135
If Juman ends up passing away,
I'll follow him.

28:46.516 --> 28:49.061
I think we should monitor him
for a couple days.

28:49.978 --> 28:53.773
Could be he's being fussy with food,
so try giving him treats he likes.

28:53.774 --> 28:56.902
If he eats his treats,
he's probably not sick.

28:57.778 --> 29:00.613
Goodness, I don't know how to thank you.

29:00.614 --> 29:04.034
Juman, thank the good doctor, okay?

29:04.826 --> 29:06.494
Okay. Goodbye, Juman.

29:07.746 --> 29:09.246
Are you okay?

29:09.247 --> 29:10.373
Oh, goodness me.

29:10.374 --> 29:11.708
:cue

29:18.006 --> 29:20.257
I was peeling onions for the dinner shift,

29:20.258 --> 29:22.636
but I ended up peeling my fingers as well.

29:26.890 --> 29:30.518
It's a big wound and it's deep,
so I think you'll need stitches.

29:30.519 --> 29:33.062
You should go to the mainland
to get it treated.

29:33.063 --> 29:34.272
The mainland?

29:34.815 --> 29:36.565
What am I going to do?

29:36.566 --> 29:38.777
We even have a group reservation today.

29:39.486 --> 29:41.947
Can't I get it treated here?

29:42.614 --> 29:44.324
It's a big wound and it's deep.

29:46.076 --> 29:48.369
If she were to file a complaint
about it leaving a scar…

29:48.370 --> 29:50.455
It's because there might be nerve damage.

29:51.957 --> 29:54.084
You'll want to get a proper checkup.

30:02.676 --> 30:04.261
I guess you like dogs, huh?

30:05.804 --> 30:06.805
No.

30:08.181 --> 30:10.267
I'm scared of them
because I got bitten once.

30:10.892 --> 30:11.893
Really?

30:13.061 --> 30:14.062
Then why…

30:15.731 --> 30:17.566
Because it seemed to bother you.

30:20.819 --> 30:21.820
Was that not the case?

30:26.283 --> 30:27.284
It's just…

30:28.827 --> 30:30.829
She reminded me of my grandma,

30:31.913 --> 30:36.626
and I felt bad for her since the dog
was her only source of warmth.

30:37.419 --> 30:38.587
That's it.

30:44.384 --> 30:47.011
I'm sorry you have to leave
before even grabbing a meal.

30:47.012 --> 30:48.429
You even got bitten by a dog.

30:48.430 --> 30:49.638
Uh…

30:49.639 --> 30:50.890
It's fine.

30:50.891 --> 30:52.975
How about you treat us
to a lot of good food

30:52.976 --> 30:54.518
- on our next visit?
- Okay.

30:54.519 --> 30:56.687
Doctor!

30:56.688 --> 30:59.940
Doctor!

30:59.941 --> 31:02.359
Oh, no.

31:02.360 --> 31:03.778
This is bad.

31:03.779 --> 31:06.363
My boy, Juman…

31:06.364 --> 31:08.616
Enough! They have to get on their boat!

31:08.617 --> 31:11.285
Oh, gosh! He's bleeding!

31:11.286 --> 31:13.579
He's going to die!

31:13.580 --> 31:15.415
- Look…
- Okay, I'll take a look.

31:18.877 --> 31:19.878
Hey,

31:20.378 --> 31:22.338
stay still.

31:22.339 --> 31:24.132
Let me take a look at you.

31:25.634 --> 31:28.178
What is it?

31:29.346 --> 31:30.889
There's a splinter stuck in him.

31:31.515 --> 31:33.558
We should remove it and stop the bleeding.

31:36.228 --> 31:37.395
But…

31:38.688 --> 31:39.689
But?

31:41.608 --> 31:43.360
I'm not sure I can do it.

31:52.119 --> 31:53.410
We don't have time.

31:53.411 --> 31:56.665
Just thirty seconds. No more.
Are you sure you can do this?

31:58.291 --> 31:59.668
Let's do this in one go.

32:01.545 --> 32:02.587
One.

32:03.463 --> 32:04.756
Two.

32:05.340 --> 32:06.633
Three. Now!

32:37.164 --> 32:39.456
- Done. We did it!
- It's done? We did it?

32:39.457 --> 32:42.334
- I got it out! We did it!
- We did it!

32:42.335 --> 32:44.753
How's my Juman doing?

32:44.754 --> 32:46.047
We got it out!

32:46.840 --> 32:50.009
-  Look!
-  Oh, thank you so much!

32:50.010 --> 32:52.052
- Thank you.
- You got it out. Wow.

32:52.053 --> 32:54.222
:cue

32:55.765 --> 32:57.976
Thank you.

33:07.694 --> 33:11.572
Hey, when will they be returning anyway?

33:11.573 --> 33:12.908
Gosh, I know.

33:13.617 --> 33:16.912
The last boat was a while ago,
so I wonder if they got on.

33:17.829 --> 33:19.414
Goodness.

33:19.956 --> 33:20.957
Oh…

33:26.213 --> 33:28.047
Yes, Public Health Center.

33:28.048 --> 33:32.009
-  Ms. Hwang…
- Hey, is something wrong?

33:32.010 --> 33:34.345
We had to treat
an urgent last-minute patient

33:34.346 --> 33:36.222
and missed the last boat.

33:36.223 --> 33:38.432
An urgent last-minute patient?

33:38.433 --> 33:41.644
Don't worry. We treated him well.

33:41.645 --> 33:44.730
Then do you have a place to stay?

33:44.731 --> 33:47.775
Yes. One of the residents here
offered a place.

33:47.776 --> 33:50.653
That's a relief.

33:50.654 --> 33:52.948
In that case, good luck with that.

33:53.531 --> 33:54.532
Mmm…

33:55.617 --> 33:56.701
What is it?

33:57.369 --> 33:59.036
Something urgent came up,

33:59.037 --> 34:01.914
so Ms. Hari and Dr. Chiyeon
missed the last boat.

34:01.915 --> 34:03.916
They'll be back tomorrow.

34:03.917 --> 34:05.167
T-Tomorrow?

34:05.168 --> 34:06.460
Yes.

34:06.461 --> 34:08.213
Wow. No way.

34:08.922 --> 34:11.508
So these things really do
happen in real life, huh?

34:12.384 --> 34:13.802
What do you mean by that?

34:14.552 --> 34:17.931
It's like something out of
a late '80s movie.

34:18.515 --> 34:20.892
- A movie?
- There he goes again, talking nonsense.

34:21.726 --> 34:22.810
Get this.

34:22.811 --> 34:26.940
A young man and woman go to an island,
and they miss the last boat.

34:27.649 --> 34:29.483
And you know what happens next?

34:29.484 --> 34:31.736
There's only one room available.

34:32.737 --> 34:33.822
Only one room…

34:35.615 --> 34:36.699
available?

34:47.585 --> 34:49.211
What to do?

34:49.212 --> 34:51.630
There's only one room left.

34:51.631 --> 34:52.840
Oh, my!

34:52.841 --> 34:55.384
The sky's grown dark
in an unfamiliar town.

34:55.385 --> 34:58.471
They're saying they only have one room.

34:59.055 --> 35:03.267
Well, I suppose it cannot be helped.

35:03.268 --> 35:06.312
They only have
each other to rely on…

35:08.189 --> 35:09.566
Mmm.

35:10.525 --> 35:12.611
Ms. Yuk!

35:14.279 --> 35:16.156
We have plenty of time to spare.

35:16.948 --> 35:18.115
Would you like a drink?

35:19.534 --> 35:22.328
Since things are awkward,

35:22.329 --> 35:25.206
they naturally gravitate towards
sharing a drink together.

35:34.716 --> 35:36.175
One glass

35:36.176 --> 35:37.469
- turns into two…
-  Cheers.

35:38.094 --> 35:40.055
Their glasses keep touching until…

35:40.930 --> 35:44.893
Dr. Chiyeon, I seem to be getting drunk.

35:46.353 --> 35:47.519
Gosh.

35:47.520 --> 35:53.233
I'm already drunk on your scent, Ms. Hari.

35:53.234 --> 35:56.738
Something else starts touching!

35:57.405 --> 35:58.657
Something else?

36:09.959 --> 36:11.920
Stop!

36:12.587 --> 36:13.962
What do you think?

36:13.963 --> 36:15.048
Not bad, huh?

36:16.091 --> 36:18.300
I'm gonna go to my room now.

36:18.301 --> 36:19.718
Okay.

36:19.719 --> 36:22.346
You're going?
Things were just getting spicy.

36:22.347 --> 36:26.809
Dr. Yong, you really put
too much thought into saying

36:26.810 --> 36:29.603
a whole lot you really don't need to say.

36:29.604 --> 36:30.813
My point exactly!

36:30.814 --> 36:33.316
I thought
it was super fun, though.
:cue

36:42.033 --> 36:44.326
What to do?

36:44.327 --> 36:46.538
I'm sorry, but we only have one room left.

36:47.163 --> 36:48.289
Uh…

36:50.625 --> 36:52.710
In that case…

36:52.711 --> 36:55.796
If it's all right with you,
would you like to stay in my room?

36:55.797 --> 36:57.756
Oh, no. That's fine.

36:57.757 --> 37:00.384
We're just grateful
that you're looking out for us.

37:00.385 --> 37:04.304
That there's my room,
so tell me if you need anything.

37:04.305 --> 37:05.306
- Okay.
- Okay.

37:17.527 --> 37:19.237
We have plenty of time to spare.

37:20.321 --> 37:21.322
Would you like a drink?

37:35.879 --> 37:38.298
They go around just fine,
even late at night.

37:44.179 --> 37:45.597
Cheers.

37:50.393 --> 37:52.562
Wow!

37:55.440 --> 37:58.233
Do you still not remember
the day we first met?

38:00.320 --> 38:01.321
Sorry.

38:02.906 --> 38:04.824
Well, that's disappointing.

38:05.575 --> 38:08.077
It was the first time in my life
I've ever been rejected.

38:09.329 --> 38:10.621
What?

38:10.622 --> 38:11.873
You rejected me,

38:12.707 --> 38:14.250
when I didn't even ask you out.

38:15.627 --> 38:17.628
What do you mean by…

38:23.092 --> 38:24.259
Hello? Emergency line?

38:24.260 --> 38:27.054
I'm the one who just called
about the motorcycle accident.

38:27.055 --> 38:29.264
Check where they are!

38:29.265 --> 38:30.891
Can you tell me where you are?

38:30.892 --> 38:32.601
Yes. She's administering CPR.

38:32.602 --> 38:35.103
I'm an intern at Yeonhui University.
I'll take over.

38:35.104 --> 38:36.773
- Okay.
-  They're almost here!

38:37.690 --> 38:39.108
EMS is on the way.

38:47.534 --> 38:49.035
The patient's breathing again.

38:50.995 --> 38:52.997
EMERGENCY MEDICAL SERVICE TEAM

39:00.004 --> 39:01.047
Good job.

39:02.715 --> 39:03.716
You too.

39:09.013 --> 39:10.098
Wait.

39:20.400 --> 39:21.526
I'm sorry.

39:22.026 --> 39:24.028
- What?
- I have a boyfriend.

39:25.196 --> 39:27.949
- Hey, wait--
- I told you I have a boyfriend.

39:29.242 --> 39:30.492
That's great.

39:30.493 --> 39:33.036
I'm sure your boyfriend
will want to reach you,

39:33.037 --> 39:34.497
- so take this with you.
- What?

39:38.835 --> 39:40.211
This is yours.

39:44.382 --> 39:45.799
Oh, my.

39:45.800 --> 39:47.593
I see. How did it…

39:47.594 --> 39:50.972
You don't seem like
love-at-first-sight material.

39:51.723 --> 39:53.098
What?

39:53.099 --> 39:55.267
Look in the mirror.
You'll see what I mean.

39:55.268 --> 39:56.394
Move aside.

40:01.274 --> 40:02.483
What's wrong with my face?

40:15.914 --> 40:17.247
You're the guy from…

40:19.042 --> 40:20.251
Right?

40:21.085 --> 40:22.629
Wow.

40:23.546 --> 40:26.673
I'm really not usually like that.

40:26.674 --> 40:29.843
I was just so out of it and that was just…

40:29.844 --> 40:32.472
- Pretty sure you're still the same.
- I'm not!

40:42.398 --> 40:44.317
It's meant to be handled with care.

40:44.984 --> 40:46.903
It should be handled with care.

40:48.696 --> 40:50.615
And we wouldn't want
anyone stealing it, so…

40:55.286 --> 40:56.787
I'll just put it over there.

40:56.788 --> 40:59.790
Hi, Hari.
How are things over there?

40:59.791 --> 41:01.792
Do you have a place to stay?

41:01.793 --> 41:04.503
Goodness. Don't worry about me.

41:04.504 --> 41:06.630
I'll take care of myself.
:cue

41:06.631 --> 41:09.717
Okay, I'm hanging up now.

41:14.555 --> 41:16.723
-  Burglar!
- Wait!

41:19.060 --> 41:21.853
Who are you?

41:21.854 --> 41:24.565
Wait! It's me.

41:28.403 --> 41:30.112
Oh, my.

41:30.113 --> 41:32.948
- You're the doctor.
- Yes.

41:32.949 --> 41:34.909
What brings you here?

41:36.160 --> 41:38.413
This. A delivery.

41:39.998 --> 41:41.082
Delivery…

41:41.874 --> 41:43.376
Oh, goodness.

41:44.377 --> 41:45.712
I'm sorry, ma'am.

41:48.423 --> 41:50.633
Come in.

41:52.677 --> 41:55.429
Sit here for a bit.

41:55.430 --> 41:56.931
I'll bring the medicine.

42:11.571 --> 42:12.572
Here.

42:13.239 --> 42:14.240
Goodness.

42:15.575 --> 42:16.659
Let me see.

42:26.544 --> 42:28.379
Goodness. That's got to hurt.

42:44.645 --> 42:47.147
ONE PAINKILLER
WHEN PAIN BECOMES UNBEARABLE

42:47.148 --> 42:49.108
TALENOL
DON'T TAKE MORE THAN FIVE

42:50.359 --> 42:54.697
But what kind of pain
is making you take so many…

42:56.991 --> 42:59.368
I didn't even get to ask you back then.

42:59.994 --> 43:01.369
Well…

43:01.370 --> 43:04.206
It's nothing.

43:04.207 --> 43:05.833
It's just migraines.

43:06.918 --> 43:09.002
It seems to be causing a lot of distress,

43:09.003 --> 43:12.339
but you shouldn't just take painkillers
because you're in pain.

43:12.340 --> 43:14.299
Don't you worry now.

43:14.300 --> 43:15.759
I know my body--

43:15.760 --> 43:17.011
Better than anyone else.

43:19.430 --> 43:23.558
But even if you may think
you know your body best,

43:23.559 --> 43:24.977
you could be wrong.

43:29.190 --> 43:30.942
Unlock your phone for me, please.

43:31.484 --> 43:32.693
What for?

43:40.368 --> 43:45.330
PH DOC DO JIUI

43:45.331 --> 43:46.415
SAVE

43:47.625 --> 43:49.251
This is my number.

43:49.252 --> 43:52.629
Give me a call
if you can't make it over to the center.

43:52.630 --> 43:53.881
Goodness me.

43:54.966 --> 43:56.300
Thank you.

43:58.761 --> 44:00.178
I'll sleep on this side.

44:00.179 --> 44:01.806
You sleep on that side.

44:02.431 --> 44:04.641
Are we really going to sleep
in the same room?

44:04.642 --> 44:06.434
Yeah, it's fine.

44:06.435 --> 44:09.813
There are bugs outside.
How can I ask you to sleep outside?

44:09.814 --> 44:11.731
Let's just make do.

44:11.732 --> 44:14.026
I didn't say
I'd be the one sleeping outside.

44:16.988 --> 44:17.989
What?

44:20.950 --> 44:22.242
I mean…

44:31.627 --> 44:33.045
What is that?

44:35.548 --> 44:37.633
Did you draw a line in case I cross it?

44:39.552 --> 44:42.722
Wow. What do you take me for?

44:43.431 --> 44:45.141
I should ask the same of you, okay?

44:46.184 --> 44:48.603
Don't you dare.
I'm going to be really mad if you do.

45:27.558 --> 45:29.310
:cue

45:38.361 --> 45:42.531
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

45:46.911 --> 45:48.453
Good morning, everyone.

45:48.454 --> 45:49.872
Good morning.

45:51.207 --> 45:52.583
Are they back yet?

45:53.167 --> 45:56.419
Dr. Chiyeon's back.
I guess you didn't run into him.

45:56.420 --> 45:57.421
No, I didn't.

46:00.216 --> 46:02.217
What about Ms. Hari?

46:02.218 --> 46:05.387
She took the day off for something.
Do you need something from her?

46:05.388 --> 46:07.390
No, it's nothing.

46:12.853 --> 46:15.730
This is PH doc Do Jiui
at the Public Health Center.

46:15.731 --> 46:18.024
Hey, I'm Ko Changmok.

46:18.025 --> 46:19.484
Excuse me?

46:19.485 --> 46:21.319
I said I'm Ko Changmok.

46:21.320 --> 46:24.572
Are you having any issues there?

46:24.573 --> 46:25.657
Sorry?

46:25.658 --> 46:30.287
I'm just calling to see
if you're having any issues over there.

46:30.288 --> 46:31.289
Who's calling?

46:31.872 --> 46:33.957
Someone's asking if we have any issues.

46:33.958 --> 46:37.252
I'm up to my neck in work!
I don't have time to deal with that crap!

46:37.253 --> 46:39.045
Tell them to stop fooling around!

46:39.046 --> 46:41.506
I'm just asking if you have any issues.

46:41.507 --> 46:44.884
We're a little busy right now,
so would you mind visiting the center?

46:44.885 --> 46:46.929
- Hello? He--
- Thank you.

46:56.605 --> 46:58.690
Goodness me,

46:58.691 --> 47:03.486
our Public Health Center
seems to be busy as hell.

47:03.487 --> 47:06.114
This is how things are between me
and our subordinates.

47:06.115 --> 47:10.076
We've done away with all formalities.
We're comfortable with each other.

47:10.077 --> 47:11.161
YEOPOONG-GUN

47:15.333 --> 47:19.045
A helicopter cuts its way
across high waves and islands.

47:19.712 --> 47:24.342
Wherever the patients may be,
a helicopter is dispatched, on the double.

47:24.925 --> 47:27.677
A mere 10 minutes
after a patient is reported,

47:27.678 --> 47:30.889
the helicopter
begins transporting the patient

47:30.890 --> 47:33.516
in a stunning display

47:33.517 --> 47:38.480
of Governor Ko Changmok's
health care modernization initiative.

47:41.734 --> 47:43.943
Now, as much as it pains me
to remember it,

47:43.944 --> 47:46.654
the image of my grandmother
grabbing my wrist

47:46.655 --> 47:49.783
and telling me that
one had no choice but to die

47:49.784 --> 47:52.952
if one were to fall sick on an island
is still seared into my heart.

47:52.953 --> 47:57.582
I promised to modernize health care
in Yeopoong-gun during my term of office,

47:57.583 --> 48:01.044
so I, Ko Changmok,
will do whatever it takes

48:01.045 --> 48:04.798
to overhaul our helipads

48:04.799 --> 48:07.342
so my grandmother's words

48:07.343 --> 48:11.222
don't apply to Yeopoong-gun, everyone!

48:14.725 --> 48:16.393
- Hey, Mr. Choi.
- Yes, sir.

48:16.394 --> 48:18.353
That place we called just now.

48:18.354 --> 48:21.856
Are you sure they recently used
a chopper to transport a patient?

48:21.857 --> 48:22.941
I'm sure of it, sir.

48:22.942 --> 48:25.735
Well, then that's no way
to respond to a call.

48:25.736 --> 48:27.195
I mean, Director,

48:27.196 --> 48:29.656
you said you strengthened
the emergency protocols.

48:29.657 --> 48:32.325
- Did you not finish what you started?
- I'm sorry, sir.

48:32.326 --> 48:33.827
Sorry just won't cut it, okay?

48:33.828 --> 48:37.330
Be sure to punish them
to uphold discipline.

48:37.331 --> 48:39.332
Yes, sir. I'll have a word with them.

48:39.333 --> 48:42.795
Just to be clear,
I told you to punish them.

49:04.316 --> 49:05.943
Perhaps you've fallen ill.

49:06.485 --> 49:08.236
Of course I've fallen ill.

49:08.237 --> 49:11.614
I'm coughing nonstop, like I told you.

49:11.615 --> 49:14.742
Not even the medicine
my daughter-in-law got me is working.

49:14.743 --> 49:17.579
Right.

49:17.580 --> 49:22.709
I'm going to have to switch
to a stronger medicine.
:cue

49:22.710 --> 49:25.420
No matter how much I take my current ones,

49:25.421 --> 49:27.422
it doesn't seem to make a difference.

49:27.423 --> 49:29.841
As I said before,
there's a variety of things

49:29.842 --> 49:32.510
- that could be causing your cough…
- For crying out loud.

49:32.511 --> 49:35.096
I told you I know all about that.

49:35.097 --> 49:39.851
Just get off my case
and give me stronger cough medicine.

49:42.730 --> 49:46.274
I'll be taking that as a yes
and leaving now.

49:54.325 --> 49:56.868
REVOPANSA PILL
30

49:56.869 --> 49:58.995
Morning and evening,
30 minutes after meals.

49:58.996 --> 50:00.748
- You know the drill, right?
- Yes.

50:01.749 --> 50:04.001
I switched to a stronger medicine.

50:09.048 --> 50:10.590
Ms. Hwang.

50:10.591 --> 50:12.884
I'm sorry,
I received the ID photo too late.

50:12.885 --> 50:14.928
You certainly took your sweet time.

50:14.929 --> 50:17.472
I see Mr. Jangsu's switching his meds.

50:17.473 --> 50:20.683
- He said he needed something stronger.
- Is he a doctor or something?

50:20.684 --> 50:22.810
Who's he to tell us
to give him stronger meds?

50:22.811 --> 50:25.104
That's how it is
with everyone here.

50:25.105 --> 50:26.773
They all know their own body best.

50:26.774 --> 50:28.566
If he knew his body so well,

50:28.567 --> 50:31.736
how did he end up getting a heart attack
and needing a stent?

50:31.737 --> 50:33.072
What a load of rubbish.

50:33.614 --> 50:34.823
A heart…

50:35.950 --> 50:37.201
Heart attack?

50:37.868 --> 50:39.202
Didn't he tell you?

50:39.203 --> 50:43.081
Mr. Jangsu also got a stent inserted
last year, just like Mr. Park.

50:43.082 --> 50:45.625
I never heard anything of the sort.

50:45.626 --> 50:47.377
That wasn't in his medical records.

50:47.378 --> 50:48.545
Scoot over.

50:48.546 --> 50:50.798
"Stent insertion, myocardial infarction."

50:51.632 --> 50:53.258
MEDICAL RECORD NOT FOUND

50:53.259 --> 50:55.760
It's not here!

50:55.761 --> 50:58.429
- I guess it hasn't been updated yet.
-  Oh, no!

50:58.430 --> 51:02.308
Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs
can cause side effects or death

51:02.309 --> 51:05.061
for patients with a history
of myocardial infarction.

51:05.062 --> 51:07.313
Is he seriously trying to ruin my life?

51:07.314 --> 51:12.777
Jangsu's Herbal Medicine.
Let it energize…

51:12.778 --> 51:14.070
Mr. Lee Jangsu!

51:14.071 --> 51:15.780
Are you kidding me right now?

51:15.781 --> 51:20.618
Black garlic extract
that's damn good for chronic fatigue,

51:20.619 --> 51:24.789
also great for hangovers,
detoxing your liver, and…

51:24.790 --> 51:26.875
Hey, Mr. Lee Jangsu!

51:27.751 --> 51:28.752
Mr. Lee Jangsu!

51:32.756 --> 51:34.048
Hey…

51:34.049 --> 51:35.843
Hey, Mr. Lee Jangsu!

51:37.886 --> 51:39.387
Mr. Lee Jangsu!

51:39.388 --> 51:41.097
♪ Twirl round and round ♪

51:41.098 --> 51:42.181
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

51:42.182 --> 51:43.766
♪ Till the night is over ♪

51:43.767 --> 51:45.518
♪ Twirl round and round ♪

51:45.519 --> 51:46.811
- Mr. Lee!
- ♪ Through the night ♪

51:46.812 --> 51:49.564
♪ And until the day goes by ♪

51:49.565 --> 51:51.233
Hey, Lee Jangsu!

51:53.527 --> 51:55.445
Hey, Lee Jangsu!

51:55.446 --> 51:56.447
Goddamn it!

51:58.532 --> 51:59.783
Mr. Lee Jangsu!

52:03.829 --> 52:04.830
I'm back!

52:07.583 --> 52:08.916
Damn.

52:08.917 --> 52:11.836
JANGSU'S HERBAL MEDICINE

52:11.837 --> 52:13.672
You're back?

52:20.512 --> 52:21.513
Seriously.

52:24.350 --> 52:25.517
Lee Jangsu!

52:30.648 --> 52:32.900
What the… Dr. Do?

52:36.737 --> 52:40.199
Mr. Lee, did you have
a heart attack before?

52:41.367 --> 52:42.700
Yes. So what?

52:42.701 --> 52:44.286
Why didn't you tell me that?

52:45.412 --> 52:48.373
I mean, it's not like telling you
would have done any good.

52:48.374 --> 52:50.583
It's not like
you're going to cure my heart!

52:50.584 --> 52:54.420
For someone with a history
of myocardial infarction, NSAIDs…

52:58.050 --> 52:59.133
The thing is…

52:59.134 --> 53:01.719
you could suffer side effects
if you take those drugs.

53:01.720 --> 53:04.682
It could even kill you,
so give me the meds right now!
:cue

53:07.518 --> 53:10.269
The meds you're taking right now.
Hand those over as well.

53:10.270 --> 53:13.064
The ones my daughter-in-law got for me?

53:13.065 --> 53:15.024
Yes, I need to know what they are.

53:15.025 --> 53:18.277
I'll go get them. Give me a second.

53:18.278 --> 53:20.531
And I prescribed all this
without knowing that!

53:27.788 --> 53:29.998
MAPRYL

53:31.166 --> 53:33.085
An ACE inhibitor.

53:33.627 --> 53:36.839
Just as I thought, the coughs
were a side effect of his meds.

53:37.965 --> 53:40.216
The reason you've been coughing,

53:40.217 --> 53:42.969
it's probably a side effect of these meds.

53:42.970 --> 53:44.470
You have to switch right now.

53:44.471 --> 53:47.348
Get a new prescription
from the hospital that did your stent.

53:47.349 --> 53:48.475
Okay.

53:59.153 --> 54:00.279
This is why…

54:04.324 --> 54:09.787
This is why patients have to be
forthcoming about their medical history.

54:09.788 --> 54:13.916
Even if you think you know your body well,
you need to consult your doctor first.

54:13.917 --> 54:15.878
That's what doctors are for!
Do you understand?

54:18.172 --> 54:19.590
I understand.

54:21.717 --> 54:22.718
I'm going now.

54:27.097 --> 54:28.390
Hey, Doctor!

54:30.392 --> 54:31.477
What is it now?

54:35.147 --> 54:37.023
Thank you.

54:37.024 --> 54:39.693
Goodness me. Thank you.

54:41.403 --> 54:47.492
I mean, you came running all this way
just to save my life, didn't you?

54:47.493 --> 54:49.994
Not even my son or my daughter-in-law

54:49.995 --> 54:51.955
would have gone to such lengths
to help me.

54:52.748 --> 54:54.624
You're absolutely right.

54:54.625 --> 54:56.959
Thank you so much.

54:56.960 --> 55:02.423
I won't touch those pills
for the rest of my life,

55:02.424 --> 55:05.385
- so don't worry about me, okay?
- Right.

55:10.557 --> 55:11.558
Okay.

55:17.856 --> 55:18.857
Take care.

55:20.817 --> 55:21.818
Goodness.

55:23.487 --> 55:25.863
Maybe I should've
given him some melons.

55:25.864 --> 55:27.449
Gosh, you're right.

55:48.428 --> 55:49.638
Hey, Doctor.

55:50.889 --> 55:52.099
Hello there.

55:53.058 --> 55:58.145
I did exactly what you told me to
and did some exercise,

55:58.146 --> 56:00.148
and my tongue's all healed now.

56:00.983 --> 56:04.861
I should invite you over
for a meal sometime.

56:06.697 --> 56:07.906
I see.

56:08.490 --> 56:10.659
Now then, you should be on your way.

56:31.388 --> 56:32.471
CLOSED FOR THE DAY

56:32.472 --> 56:35.308
VISITING A MAINLAND HOSPITAL
DUE TO A HAND INJURY

56:35.309 --> 56:37.728
CLIFFSIDE RAW FISH RESTAURANT
:cue

56:55.954 --> 56:57.413
Gosh.

56:57.414 --> 56:59.999
Dr. Do, are you okay?

57:00.000 --> 57:02.627
I'll prescribe a different medicine
for Mr. Lee.

57:02.628 --> 57:03.754
Right.

57:04.671 --> 57:07.174
Goodness me.
Mr. Park, what brings you here?

57:12.679 --> 57:14.306
Have some of this.

57:15.432 --> 57:17.267
Oh, my!

57:17.934 --> 57:18.935
- Goodness!
- Sorry?

57:20.395 --> 57:22.229
Goodness gracious!

57:22.230 --> 57:23.731
Or toss it if you don't want it.

57:23.732 --> 57:24.941
Dr. Do.

57:28.070 --> 57:30.113
What's going on?

57:31.031 --> 57:33.574
I went to the hospital to look into it.

57:33.575 --> 57:36.077
Turns out the insurance company
tried to cheat him.

57:38.163 --> 57:41.040
They rejected the claim
for Mr. Park's stent procedure

57:41.041 --> 57:44.544
for myocardial infarction,
classifying it as angina instead.

57:45.754 --> 57:47.923
And I just took their word for it.

57:49.508 --> 57:51.759
They argued that
it wasn't myocardial infarction

57:51.760 --> 57:53.969
because there was no ST segment elevation,

57:53.970 --> 57:55.638
but his report clearly states

57:55.639 --> 57:58.349
that it was a non-ST-segment elevation
myocardial infarction,

57:58.350 --> 58:00.226
so it was indeed a myocardial infarction.

58:00.227 --> 58:02.228
That means you can claim your payout.

58:02.229 --> 58:03.312
Right.

58:03.313 --> 58:04.522
It may take a while,

58:04.523 --> 58:07.566
but you can still get your payout
if you file for compensation

58:07.567 --> 58:10.528
with the Korea Consumer Agency
and make an insurance claim.

58:10.529 --> 58:13.699
Wow, so you went there in person
to look into everything?

58:14.282 --> 58:17.201
- Yeah.
- Goodness me, you precious thing.

58:17.202 --> 58:20.538
You really were trained
at a big university hospital.

58:20.539 --> 58:24.291
How are you so smart?
This is such great news.

58:24.292 --> 58:25.584
I should get going now.

58:25.585 --> 58:28.714
Okay, we won't walk you out.

58:29.631 --> 58:31.006
And…

58:31.007 --> 58:34.261
my wife will be bringing lunch
for the center tomorrow.

58:36.012 --> 58:37.638
I told her to bring meat dishes.

58:37.639 --> 58:38.640
Okay.

58:39.725 --> 58:40.934
Dr. Do Jiui…

58:43.645 --> 58:45.313
enjoy the food, okay?

58:47.065 --> 58:48.692
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

58:50.277 --> 58:53.029
- You precious thing.
-  I did good, didn't I?

58:54.614 --> 58:55.698
Let me prepare those.

58:55.699 --> 58:57.908
Sure. Just how many are there?

58:57.909 --> 58:59.619
We're gonna have ourselves a feast.

59:14.760 --> 59:18.263
I'LL BE OUT FOR A WHILE
I'LL LEAVE IT UP TO YOUR CONSCIENCE

59:35.113 --> 59:36.656
Were you waiting for me?

59:37.449 --> 59:38.616
Me, wait for you?

59:38.617 --> 59:41.578
Not at all. I was just…

59:42.996 --> 59:45.373
You look like
you've got something to say.

59:48.210 --> 59:49.502
If not, never mind.

59:49.503 --> 59:50.921
Thank you.

59:52.172 --> 59:53.547
:cue

59:53.548 --> 59:55.550
Was that so hard?

59:58.970 --> 01:00:00.806
Care to join me for some beer?

01:00:06.228 --> 01:00:07.229
Cheers.

01:00:13.944 --> 01:00:16.238
There's something I want to ask you.

01:00:16.863 --> 01:00:17.864
Mmm.

01:00:19.616 --> 01:00:21.618
Why did you send this to me?

01:00:23.161 --> 01:00:25.621
I actually sent that by accident.

01:00:25.622 --> 01:00:28.958
I had a good laugh.
Isn't it hilarious?

01:00:28.959 --> 01:00:30.709
Delete it.

01:00:30.710 --> 01:00:33.129
No. I'm going to look at it
whenever I feel down.

01:00:41.680 --> 01:00:44.224
You should also take a look
and get a laugh out of it.

01:00:46.393 --> 01:00:47.560
Okay?

01:00:47.561 --> 01:00:48.562
Okay.

01:00:50.438 --> 01:00:53.233
You've had a dark cloud
hanging over your head all day.

01:00:57.696 --> 01:00:59.155
Did something happen?

01:01:02.701 --> 01:01:04.411
Well…

01:01:08.498 --> 01:01:10.792
I prescribed an NSAID to a patient

01:01:12.127 --> 01:01:14.753
with a history
of myocardial infarction today.

01:01:14.754 --> 01:01:15.755
What?

01:01:16.256 --> 01:01:18.675
Do they know they shouldn't take it?

01:01:19.509 --> 01:01:23.012
That's why I ran after him
to tell him not to take it.

01:01:23.013 --> 01:01:24.431
I see.

01:01:25.015 --> 01:01:27.017
Because taking it might have killed him.

01:01:30.979 --> 01:01:32.188
But here's the thing…

01:01:34.065 --> 01:01:37.110
I wasn't worried about the patient
as I was chasing after him.

01:01:38.820 --> 01:01:40.238
I only worried about myself.

01:01:42.657 --> 01:01:45.409
If someone were to find out
I prescribed the wrong meds,

01:01:45.410 --> 01:01:48.996
they could have filed a complaint,
which would lead to disciplinary action

01:01:48.997 --> 01:01:52.000
and me getting trapped on this island.

01:01:55.837 --> 01:01:57.881
I ran after him to save myself.

01:02:01.968 --> 01:02:02.969
But…

01:02:06.598 --> 01:02:08.600
the patient thanked me.

01:02:11.144 --> 01:02:12.729
For saving his life.

01:02:16.816 --> 01:02:20.111
I lashed out so many times
because people looked down on PH docs…

01:02:22.489 --> 01:02:24.115
but it turns out I was the one…

01:02:26.785 --> 01:02:28.244
who looked down on myself most.

01:02:30.038 --> 01:02:31.247
Despite being a doctor…

01:02:33.333 --> 01:02:35.543
I decided to do nothing.

01:02:44.594 --> 01:02:45.720
Doctor…

01:02:46.846 --> 01:02:48.431
come with me.

01:02:49.265 --> 01:02:50.266
What?

01:02:51.226 --> 01:02:53.728
- Come on.
- What? Where…

01:02:54.270 --> 01:02:55.772
You'll see when we get there.
:cue

01:03:00.026 --> 01:03:02.152
What on earth are you looking for?

01:03:02.153 --> 01:03:04.905
Just give it a second.

01:03:04.906 --> 01:03:06.908
There's something I want to show you.

01:03:07.534 --> 01:03:09.576
I get that, but what is it?

01:03:09.577 --> 01:03:13.123
It's not something
you can come across that easily, but…

01:03:15.333 --> 01:03:16.793
That's odd.

01:03:19.504 --> 01:03:22.716
They should be showing up right about now.

01:03:27.303 --> 01:03:29.305
I'm going to climb my way down now.

01:03:32.559 --> 01:03:34.102
Wait!

01:03:35.437 --> 01:03:36.813
Come here!

01:03:37.856 --> 01:03:39.732
What is it?

01:03:39.733 --> 01:03:40.817
Be quiet.

01:04:07.677 --> 01:04:09.928
I've never seen fireflies before.

01:04:09.929 --> 01:04:11.221
Really?

01:04:11.222 --> 01:04:13.850
Wow.

01:04:16.895 --> 01:04:18.104
What do you think?

01:04:18.855 --> 01:04:20.065
Aren't they beautiful?

01:04:23.735 --> 01:04:25.652
What did I tell you?

01:04:25.653 --> 01:04:27.655
I told you they'd show up soon.

01:04:31.826 --> 01:04:32.994
They're beautiful, right?

01:04:46.174 --> 01:04:47.509
By the way, Dr. Do…

01:04:50.887 --> 01:04:52.222
this island

01:04:53.515 --> 01:04:55.808
and the people here are just as beautiful

01:04:55.809 --> 01:04:58.436
when you look at them from up close.

01:05:04.234 --> 01:05:08.613
I'm sorry to have to keep telling you
to bear with it all the time.

01:05:10.657 --> 01:05:13.868
But you doctors are the only ones
the people here can depend on

01:05:14.869 --> 01:05:16.538
when they get sick.

01:05:19.249 --> 01:05:23.001
So please go easy on them. Okay?

01:05:35.390 --> 01:05:38.226
Dr. Chiyeon, do you want to have a beer?

01:05:38.977 --> 01:05:41.478
No, I'm going to sleep early.

01:05:41.479 --> 01:05:43.105
I didn't get any sleep last night.

01:05:45.900 --> 01:05:49.278
So you didn't
get any sleep on Madeokdo?

01:05:49.279 --> 01:05:50.280
No.

01:05:51.239 --> 01:05:52.406
Have a good rest.

01:05:55.368 --> 01:05:57.036
I knew it.

01:05:59.956 --> 01:06:01.749
What's got everyone so worked up?

01:06:03.459 --> 01:06:04.960
Stop everything. Major PSA.

01:06:04.961 --> 01:06:07.546
Has a nurse recently joined
any of your health centers?

01:06:07.547 --> 01:06:10.299
Apparently, she's notorious
for being a doctor hunter!

01:06:10.300 --> 01:06:11.551
A doctor hunter?

01:06:12.135 --> 01:06:13.635
Hmm?

01:06:13.636 --> 01:06:16.221
Do you mean
the short-haired gold digger?

01:06:16.222 --> 01:06:18.849
The one from Asong Hospital,
with the mole on her nose!

01:06:18.850 --> 01:06:21.143
I heard about her from an older colleague.

01:06:21.144 --> 01:06:23.479
Asong Hospital's infamous nurse
who targets doctors!
:cue

01:06:27.025 --> 01:06:30.861
A nurse from Asong Hospital?

01:06:30.862 --> 01:06:32.529
Ms. Hari here is an intellectual

01:06:32.530 --> 01:06:36.283
who used to work
in a university hospital's ER.

01:06:36.284 --> 01:06:40.330
Not just any hospital,
but Asong Hospital…

01:06:42.415 --> 01:06:43.833
Could it be…

01:06:46.502 --> 01:06:47.795
Yuk Hari?

01:06:54.469 --> 01:06:56.304
Can I ask you something?

01:06:57.013 --> 01:06:58.139
Mmm.

01:07:01.017 --> 01:07:02.268
Why did you go to Madeokdo…

01:07:03.895 --> 01:07:07.232
with Dr. Hyeon Chiyeon?

01:07:08.399 --> 01:07:09.400
Oh.

01:07:10.193 --> 01:07:12.653
How could I have gone there with you?

01:07:12.654 --> 01:07:14.197
It's not within walking distance.

01:07:16.783 --> 01:07:19.077
It's over an hour away by boat.

01:07:21.621 --> 01:07:22.830
Ah.

01:07:26.209 --> 01:07:28.336
So you were looking out for me.

01:07:29.796 --> 01:07:31.005
I didn't even realize that.

01:07:34.968 --> 01:07:37.011
But I kind of regret it.

01:07:41.975 --> 01:07:43.810
Maybe I shouldn't have looked out for you…

01:07:45.770 --> 01:07:48.273
and just gone there with you.

01:07:59.117 --> 01:08:00.285
Next time…

01:08:02.620 --> 01:08:04.247
do you want to go with me?

01:08:32.150 --> 01:08:35.569
EVEN IF YOU THINK
YOU KNOW YOUR BODY WELL,

01:08:35.570 --> 01:08:40.490
YOU NEED TO CONSULT
YOUR DOCTOR FIRST

01:08:40.491 --> 01:08:45.705
THAT'S WHAT DOCTORS ARE FOR

01:09:00.303 --> 01:09:04.223
YOU HAVE TO BE QUIET TO
SEE THE FIREFLIES

01:09:12.315 --> 01:09:15.234
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

01:09:16.069 --> 01:09:20.822
So you're saying Dr. Hyeon Chiyeon is
going out with Ms. Yuk Hari, huh?

01:09:20.823 --> 01:09:23.241
You could see hearts in their eyes.

01:09:23.242 --> 01:09:25.827
Looks like we might be having
a wedding on Pyeondongdo!

01:09:25.828 --> 01:09:27.954
It didn't seem to be just a rumor.

01:09:27.955 --> 01:09:29.373
Does it bother you that much?

01:09:29.374 --> 01:09:30.957
I had no idea

01:09:30.958 --> 01:09:32.460
that you and Dr. Chiyeon were…

01:09:33.503 --> 01:09:35.838
So you were scared
that I'd get my hooks in?

01:09:36.672 --> 01:09:38.632
I'm telling you,

01:09:38.633 --> 01:09:40.385
she's definitely gotten her hooks in!

01:09:45.098 --> 01:09:47.100
Translated by Yoon Hyuk Park
